app "LiveConversationGrok" do
  description do
    en <<~TEXT
    Continuous voice conversation over xAI's Grok realtime API (speech-to-speech). Press Start and talk — turns are detected automatically until you press Stop. Headphones are recommended: with speakers, the assistant's voice can leak into the microphone and trigger false turns; in noisy environments Grok may transcribe fluent but incorrect text. Audio is sent directly to the provider (Privacy Filter does not apply). Billing runs per session minute — idle time included — and a running cost estimate is shown while the session is open. Tools (current time, Python code, Knowledge Base search, web search) are available when you switch them on; there is no text input. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=live-conversation" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT
    ja <<~TEXT
    xAI Grok realtime API（speech-to-speech）による連続音声会話。Start を押して話しかけると、Stop までターンが自動で続きます。ヘッドホンの使用を推奨します（スピーカーだとアシスタントの音声がマイクに回り込み、誤ってターンが始まることがあります）。騒がしい環境では、Grok は流暢だが不正確なテキストを転写することがあります。音声はプロバイダに直接送信されます（Privacy Filter 非対応）。課金はセッションの分単位で、無音の時間も対象です。セッション中は料金の目安が画面に表示されます。ツール（現在時刻・Python コード実行・Knowledge Base 検索・ウェブ検索）は、オンにしたときのみ使えます。テキスト入力はありません。 <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=live-conversation" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT
  end

  icon "comments"

  display_name "Live Conversation"

  system_prompt <<~PROMPT
  You are a friendly conversation partner speaking with the user by voice.
  Keep responses short and natural for speech — usually one or two sentences.
  Follow the user's language. Do not use markdown, lists, or code in your
  speech; talk the way a person talks.
  If you could not hear or understand the user clearly, say so briefly and
  ask them to repeat. Never guess at what they said, and never invent
  content that was not actually shared — there are no images, photos, or
  files in this conversation, only voice.
  The user's speech may reach you split into fragments when they pause
  mid-sentence. If an utterance sounds unfinished, do not answer it fully:
  give a minimal acknowledgement or briefly invite them to continue. When
  the next utterance arrives, treat it as the continuation of the same
  thought, not a new topic.
  If you say you are going to use a tool, wait for the tool's result
  before answering — do not answer from memory first and correct yourself
  afterwards.
  PROMPT

  llm do
    provider "xai"
    model ["grok-voice-think-fast-2.0"]
  end

  features do
    # Declares this as a speech-to-speech app: the frontend switches to the
    # Live Conversation UI (Start/Stop, no text input) and the model list is
    # pinned to the MDSL declaration above (show-all is ignored).
    speech_to_speech true
    # Greeting toggle: ON = the assistant greets when a fresh conversation
    # starts; OFF = start listening silently. Resume never greets.
    initiate_from_assistant true
    # The Library search TOOL is suppressed here: Live Conversation tools are
    # opt-in through the app's own Tools toggle (library_search is offered
    # there), and with the toggle off the realtime session config carries no
    # tools key at all — that wire invariant is pinned in the handler spec.
    # Conversations still save to the Library like any app.
    library_search false
    # Server-VAD tuning (same MDSL vocabulary as the OpenAI variant; the xAI
    # payload builder validates against xAI's ranges — threshold 0.1–0.9,
    # silence 0–10000ms — and does not send unsupported keys).
    sts_vad_threshold 0.65
    sts_vad_silence_ms 1000
    disabled !CONFIG["XAI_API_KEY"]
  end
end
